message: Please cite the paper; this repository supplies its source.
type: software
title: "Forgetting under noise is undecidable"
version: 2.1.0
date-released: '2026-11-12'
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24176024"
license: [CC-BY-4.0, MIT, Apache-2.0]
authors: [{"family-names": "Douglas", "given-names": "Seth", "orcid": "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4708-3252"}, {"family-names": "Mghirbi", "given-names": "Nidhal", "orcid": "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6534-1118"}]
keywords: ["probabilistic cellular automata", "ergodicity", "undecidability", "positive rates", "Wang tiles", "Toom contours", "existential pebble games", "local consistency", "space-time Gibbs measures", "noise", "Gibbs measures", "weak spatial mixing", "Lean"]
abstract: "A natural noisy Wang rule on Z^4 is ergodic exactly when its finite raw tile set does not tile the plane. A cardinal checker and a fixed 512-of-768 quorum use the tiles themselves and one blank. A transverse-quorum lift of Kari's nilpotency reduction gives the same equivalence on Z^3 for north/east deterministic tile sets. At every 0 < epsilon <= 382205952^(-33720), non-tiling inputs in either family have all-input nonconstancy probability on a finite window F at most |F| C_R exp(-t/4), with universal exponent and an effectively findable input-dependent prefactor uniform in epsilon. Tiling gives two invariant laws; a one-tile example shows why the rate requires non-tiling. Ergodicity is undecidable at one fixed rational rate in both families. A saturation theorem explains the earlier budget-only dimension obstruction. The retained Z^6 natural rule also has all-Gibbs uniqueness and robustness. Its Theorems D and A are verified in Lean; the Z^4 and Z^3 results, including the new rate, are not formalized. The inspector theory and Z^8 machine-family Lean core are retained."
